    "result_text": "Owner responses now include a `timezone` field, and the test suite passes: all 17 tests across 5 classes, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion`.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`**: added a `REGION_TIMEZONES` table (NSW \u2192 `Australia/Sydney`, VIC \u2192 `Australia/Melbourne`, QLD \u2192 `Australia/Brisbane`) and a `toTimezone(owner)` method that looks up the owner's existing `locality` in it. `toOwnerDto` now fills `timezone` from that method.\n- **`openapi.yml`**: added a read-only `timezone` string to the `Owner` schema, describing the table. The generated `OwnerDto` gets the field from there.\n\nSince `timezone` is based on `locality`, it follows the same precedence: customer-code region first, then postcode range, then city. If the locality is `UNKNOWN` or anything else outside the table, `timezone` is null.",
